<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">al-Amin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/787">787</a>–<a href="/years/813">813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad al-Amin (caliph)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Amin was the sixth Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a>, who reigned from 809 to 813. His attempt to exclude his half-brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mamun">al-Ma'mun</a>, governor of Khurasan, from the succession led to a civil war, the Fourth Fitna. Al-Ma'mun's general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahir-ibn-husayn">Tahir ibn Husayn</a> defeated al-Amin's armies and besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, and al-Amin was killed after the city fell in 813.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-amin.jpg" alt="al-Amin" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DrFO.Jr.Tn · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbasid_Dinar_-_Al_Amin_-_195_AH_(811_AD).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Only an Abbasid could be caliph, but no rule fixed the succession: caliphs named heirs among their sons and brothers, and the choice was often fought over, as in the civil war of 811–813 between <b>al-Amin</b> and al-Ma’mun.</blockquote><a href="/societies/abbasid-caliphate">Social Hierarchy of the Abbasid Caliphate</a></li><li><blockquote>Tahir ibn Husayn, a Persian general of Khurasani origin, defeated the caliph <b>al-Amin's</b> armies in the civil war of 811 to 813 and secured the throne for al-Ma'mun.</blockquote><a href="/state/tahirid-dynasty">Tahirid dynasty</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Al-Rusafa, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=33.33,44.42&amp;year=803" aria-label="Al-Rusafa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5686 954 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of al-Amin"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6136 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6136 1224h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=33.33,44.42&amp;year=803">What was here in 803 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
